{"id": "9fe3a7c9-69d7-4710-b28e-239660b9461c", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I think I have enough to answer now. For container-based deployments with a custom Dockerfile, the runtime doesn't auto-inject OTEL instrumentation the way CLI-based deployments do, so I'd need to add aws-opentelemetry-distro to requirements and launch with opentelemetry-instrument wrapping the main entrypoint.

The most likely culprit I can pinpoint concretely is that Transaction Search isn't enabled, which blocks spans from reaching the X-Ray span ingestion path, but there's real uncertainty since I can't see their actual account setup. I should present multiple hypotheses clearly labeled, mention checking DISABLE_ADOT_OBSERVABILITY, trace header propagation, and log-trace correlation, while being upfront I haven't inspected their environment and offering a read-only check.

